Subject: [PATCH] vm: free only what a failed copy owns

A VM copy shares the VMG IFO and the dvd reader with the VM it copies.
When vm_new_copy() failed after the copy, vm_free_vm() closed both, and
the source VM went on with freed memory.
---
 src/vm/vm.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/vm/vm.c b/src/vm/vm.c
index 9276c912bc..1091e1c0f4 100644
--- a/src/vm/vm.c
+++ b/src/vm/vm.c
@@ -526,7 +526,7 @@ vm_t *vm_new_copy(vm_t *source) {
 
 fail:
   if (target != NULL)
-    vm_free_vm(target);
+    vm_free_copy(target);
 
   return NULL;
 }
